{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/math\/compiletimesafety"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathUnit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" carries a compile-time dimension type through its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Dimension","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" associated type. That type is a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/DimensionProtocol","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"-conforming"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"struct from the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" namespace, such as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/length","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/time","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Because the compiler can see this type, it can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reject dimension mismatches "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"when you build your app"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of when it runs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Historically, dimensions were only checked at runtime. With compile-time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constraints, a function that declares "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“only lengths, please”"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" is enforced by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the Swift type checker."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Constrain-a-Generic-to-a-Dimension","text":"Constrain a Generic to a Dimension","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Write a generic function or protocol requirement over a unit type "},{"code":"U: MathUnit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then constrain "},{"code":"U.Dimension","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with a "},{"code":"where","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" clause:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import Math","","\/\/ This method only accepts quantities of length.","func measureDistance<U: MathUnit>(_ distance: Quantity<U>) -> Bool","where U.Dimension == MathDimension.length {","    distance.value > 0","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Passing-the-Correct-Units","text":"Passing the Correct Units","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The built-in units in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Units","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" are already parameterized by their dimension."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Passing a length unit compiles cleanly:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let radius = Quantity(value: 500, unit: Units.meter)","measureDistance(radius) \/\/ Compiles perfectly! ✅"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Preventing-Mismatched-Units","text":"Preventing Mismatched Units","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Passing a quantity of a different dimension is a compile-time error:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let timeLimit = Quantity(value: 30, unit: Units.minute)","measureDistance(timeLimit) \/\/ ✗ ERROR: 'time' is not 'length'"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Runtime-Checks-for-Dynamic-Dimensions","text":"Runtime Checks for Dynamic Dimensions","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not every quantity has a static dimension. Custom dimensions created at runtime"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CustomDimensions","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/unknown","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as their type-level"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parameter. For those, the compiler can’t help—so "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps its runtime"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"safety net. Operations that combine quantities verify that dimensions match and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"raise a runtime "},{"code":"preconditionFailure","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" if they don’t:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let usdDimension = PhysicalDimension(exponents: [\"USD\": 1])","let usdUnit = NamedUnit<MathDimension.unknown>(","    symbol: \"$\", dimension: usdDimension, converter: LinearConverter(coefficient: 1.0)",")","","let userDimension = PhysicalDimension(exponents: [\"user\": 1])","let userUnit = NamedUnit<MathDimension.unknown>(","    symbol: \"user\", dimension: userDimension, converter: LinearConverter(coefficient: 1.0)",")","","\/\/ Traps at runtime: USD ≠ users","let revenue = Quantity(value: 100, unit: usdUnit) + Quantity(value: 3, unit: userUnit)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Applying-Constraints-at-the-Protocol-Level","text":"Applying Constraints at the Protocol Level","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can attach the same constraint to a protocol so every conformer enforces it:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["protocol DistanceMeasurer {","    func measure<U: MathUnit>(_ distance: Quantity<U>) -> Double","    where U.Dimension == MathDimension.length","}","","\/\/ All built-in length units satisfy this automatically:","struct RangeFinder: DistanceMeasurer {","    func measure<U: MathUnit>(_ distance: Quantity<U>) -> Double","    where U.Dimension == MathDimension.length {","        distance.converted(to: Units.meter).value","    }","}","","let width = Quantity(value: 10, unit: Units.foot)","RangeFinder().measure(width) \/\/ 3.048"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Whats-Next","text":"What’s Next?","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"See the full list of compile-time dimensions in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Combine compile-time safety with your own domain in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CustomDimensions","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Math"}],"title":"Compile-Time Dimension Type Safety"},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompileTimeSafety"},"abstract":[{"text":"Use generic constraints to make sure your APIs only ever receive the right kind of quantity.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Extending the Framework","generated":true,"anchor":"Extending-the-Framework","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CustomDimensions"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math"]]},"references":{"doc://Math/documentation/Math":{"type":"topic","title":"Math","url":"\/documentation\/math","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math","abstract":[{"text":"Perform type-safe dimensional analysis and unit conversion in your Swift app.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/MathUnit":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A unit of measurement, such as a meter, a second, or a US dollar."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MathUnit","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MathUnit","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MathUnit","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathUnit","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/math\/mathunit"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/MathDimension/unknown":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"unknown"}],"title":"MathDimension.unknown","url":"\/documentation\/math\/mathdimension\/unknown","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"unknown"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The compile-time dimension type used for dimensions that don’t have a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"static type, such as custom dimensions created at runtime."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/unknown","role":"symbol"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/Units":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A namespace of ready-made units for every dimension in the framework."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Units","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Units","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Units"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Units","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/math\/units","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/MathDimension":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A namespace containing type-level structures for compile-time physical dimension verification."}],"title":"MathDimension","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/math\/mathdimension","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MathDimension"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"MathDimension","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/MathDimension/time":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/time","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"MathDimension.time","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"time"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"time"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The compile-time dimension type representing time."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/math\/mathdimension\/time"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/DimensionProtocol":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DimensionProtocol"}],"url":"\/documentation\/math\/dimensionprotocol","title":"DimensionProtocol","abstract":[{"text":"A protocol representing a type-level identifier for a physical dimension.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/DimensionProtocol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DimensionProtocol"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/CustomDimensions":{"url":"\/documentation\/math\/customdimensions","title":"Custom Dimensions and Units","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CustomDimensions","abstract":[{"text":"Extend ","type":"text"},{"code":"Math","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with your own physical dimensions and units—currency, points, gameplay metrics, or anything else your app measures."}],"type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/MathDimension/length":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"length"}],"url":"\/documentation\/math\/mathdimension\/length","title":"MathDimension.length","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The compile-time dimension type representing length."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/length","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"length","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"}}}